{
  "name": "Block bounced and opted-out addresses everywhere and flag them in HubSpot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Block bounced and opted-out addresses everywhere and flag them in HubSpot\n\n### How it works\nOne bounce or opt-out should count everywhere. Argorant already stops the campaign that bounced or got the opt-out. This workflow goes further: it blocks the address for every campaign of your workspace, flags the contact in HubSpot with a custom property (bounced or unsubscribed), and appends a row to a log sheet with the date, address, reason and campaign, so you can review deliverability.\n\nNo credits are used.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Activate the trigger with your Argorant credential. Argorant webhooks come with the Pro plan, and your n8n needs a public HTTPS address.\n4. In HubSpot, create a contact property with the internal name argorant_status (single line text). Add a HubSpot credential.\n5. Create a sheet with the columns date, email, reason, campaign_id and pick it in **Log the event**.\n\n### Customization\nBlock the whole domain for hard bounces, or skip the CRM step.",
        "height": 609,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "f42c7191-ac38-4601-a4ac-4ac4eaf112cb",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Block\nThe address leaves every campaign of the workspace and is never added again.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "74ff7432-0e1c-4452-9e0b-5c435c5cff36",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Record\nThe CRM flag and the log keep your other tools in line.",
